# How the demo decides who may open it. Copy this file to .env only for local work.
#
# VITE_LOGIN=access   The hosted demo. Cloudflare Access sits in front of every address and
#                     emails a one-time code to approved addresses before any file is sent.
#                     The app has no password of its own in this mode. `npm run build:cloudflare`
#                     sets this for you, so nothing needs to go in a file for Cloudflare.
# VITE_LOGIN=local    Your own machine (the default). A username and password checked in the
#                     page itself, so anyone who reads the code can get past it. Fine for
#                     `npm run dev`; never for the public internet (`npm run build` refuses).
VITE_LOGIN=local

# Local mode only. The default is username demo, password demo. To use your own password,
# hash it with:  npm run hash-password -- "your password"   and paste the result below.
VITE_DEMO_USERNAME=demo
VITE_DEMO_PASSWORD_SHA256=

# Vardil Works (the level above the managing director, Vardil staff only). The hosted build
# includes it; on your own computer set VITE_STAFF=1 in .env.local to see it. Never set it for
# the shareable single-file preview. Which email domains count as Vardil staff on the hosted demo:
# VITE_STAFF=1
# VITE_STAFF_DOMAINS=vardil.com
